  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most informative first step is to establish a simple, reliable baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the search space: it uses a standard, low-risk encoder (PCA), the simplest profile setting, and no aggregation or fusion complexity. This gives us a clear accuracy floor for the RNA modality. In subsequent experiments, we can test image-only (config_010/013) to compare modalities, then explore better RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt) or multimodal fusion, always benchmarking against this baseline. Starting simple minimizes the risk of confounding multiple design choices and provides the reference point needed to interpret all later results within the 10-experiment budget."
